= Open Questions

This chapter gathers the questions not yet answered about names, dates and family ties. Each entry says what is known, what is still unclear, and what kind of record might help. If you know something about any of them, or have letters, photographs or papers that might bear on them, please tell Tamsin.

== Penhallow and Treloar

John Penhallow's baptism names his parents as Richard and Grace Penhallow of Trewellard.#src("john-penhallow::john-baptism-1845") No second record has yet confirmed them, so they are not entered as ancestors. A search of the St Just burials up to 1868 did not find Richard, so he may have outlived John's departure.

The family's arrival in America is dated two ways. The county album says they came in 1867, while the passenger list and John's obituary say 1868.#src("john-penhallow::john-album-1904")#src("john-penhallow::john-arrival-1868") The album was written long after the event, so this book follows 1868.

Elizabeth's birthplace, Camborne, comes from a journal article that does not cite the register entry it used.#src("elizabeth-trembath::elizabeth-birth-camborne") Her baptism in the Camborne registers would settle it.

Edith Rowe's birthplace, Rowe's Diggings, has not been found on any map or in any gazetteer.#src("edith-may-rowe::edith-birth-marriage-register") It may have been a local name for a mining camp. An online tree names her parents as Samuel Rowe and Jane Hocking, but it gives no sources.#src("edith-may-rowe::edith-parents-tree")

Mary Treloar's maiden name is unknown.#src("mary-treloar::mary-treloar-list") Her marriage record, or the full census entry for the Treloar household, could name her parents. The typed Treloar list that supplies several dates has no known author.#src("thomas-treloar::thomas-birth-list")

== Solberg and Kessler

Almost everything known about the Solbergs comes from Ruth Solberg's memories.#src("olaf-solberg::olaf-birth") Olaf's birth record or an early Minneapolis census could name his parents and show where in Norway they came from.

Herman Kessler's parents are not yet identified.#src("herman-kessler::herman-census-1940") Ruth believed they came from Germany, but no record seen so far says so.
